1178	     * target's right subtree (successor->parent != target). rb_delete
1179	     * must first splice the successor out of its own spot (promoting the
1180	     * successor's right child -- a minimum node never has a left child),
1181	     * then move the successor into target's slot with BOTH of target's
1182	     * original children reattached. The successor is given its own right
1183	     * child here so that promotion is actually exercised, not just left
1184	     * nil by coincidence. */
